  "details": "<p>The <em>Barrington Atlas Directory</em> and PECS follow 19th century European travelers' reports in associating this site with the modern Turkish name Hay\u0131tl\u0131, but that name does not appear in more modern gazetteers.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Ruins of an ancient town located in a now-uninhabited forest area near the modern Turkish town of Kapakl\u0131 in the Demre district of Antalya province. Its ancient name is known only from fragmentary epigraphic sources of the Hellenistic period, but archaeological investigation has demonstrated occupation and development from the 3rd century BCE through late antiquity, with some modest habitation continuing in the medieval period.",
